{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-90573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Is the function $h(x,y,z)={x}^{3}y+x{y}^{3}-8{z}^{3}$ homogeneous? If so, what is its degree?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A function $h(x,y,z)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\nh(tx,ty,tz)={t}^{n}h(x,y,z).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $h(tx,ty,tz),$ and then we simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}h(x,y,z)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(tx,ty,tz) & =(tx)^{3}(ty)+(tx)(ty)^{3}-8(tz)^{3} \\\\  & ={t}^{4}{x}^{3}y+{t}^{4}x{y}^{3}-8{t}^{3}{z}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt's impossible to write this as\n\n$$\n{t}^{n}h(x,y,z)={t}^{n}({x}^{3}y+x{y}^{3}-8{z}^{3})\n$$\n\nand so $h(x,y,z)$ is not homogeneous." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97da43b2889dff1e9a1bf9fcf026f3916bef5db7bb71f229952d30ad5f6fda26"} {"question" "q-90573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Homogeneous of degree $1$"] ["text" "Homogeneous of degree $2$"] ["text" "Homogeneous of degree $3$"] ["text" "Homogeneous of degree $4$"] ["text" "Not homogeneous"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "Not homogeneous"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-79577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Is the function $f(x,y,z)=2xyz-{y}^{3}+{y}^{2}z$ homogeneous? If so, what is its degree?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-79577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A function $f(x,y,z)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty,tz)={t}^{n}f(x,y,z).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $f(tx,ty,tz),$ and then we simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}f(x,y)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty,tz) & =2(tx)(ty)(tz)-(ty)^{3}+(ty)^{2}(tz) \\\\  & =2{t}^{3}xyz-{t}^{3}{y}^{3}+{t}^{3}{y}^{2}z \\\\  & ={t}^{3}(2xyz-{y}^{3}+{y}^{2}z) \\\\  & ={t}^{3}f(x,y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty,tz)={t}^{3}f(x,y,z)\n$$\n\nand so the degree of the homogeneous function $f(x,y,z)$ is $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-79577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97da43b2889dff1e9a1bf9fcf026f3916bef5db7bb71f229952d30ad5f6fda26"} {"question" "q-79577" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-79577" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Homogeneous of degree $1$"] ["text" "Homogeneous of degree $2$"] ["text" "Homogeneous of degree $3$"] ["text" "Homogeneous of degree $4$"] ["text" "Not homogeneous"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-79577" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "Homogeneous of degree $3$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Is the function $g(x,y)=2{x}^{3}+3{y}^{2}$ homogeneous? If so, what is its degree?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\ng(tx,ty)={t}^{n}g(x,y).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $g(tx,ty),$ and then we try to simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}g(x,y)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(tx,ty) & =2(tx)^{3}+3(ty)^{2} \\\\  & =2{t}^{3}{x}^{3}+3{t}^{2}{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt's impossible to write this as\n\n$$\n{t}^{n}g(x,y)={t}^{n}(2{x}^{3}+3{y}^{2})\n$$\n\nand so $g(x,y)$ is not homogeneous." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97da43b2889dff1e9a1bf9fcf026f3916bef5db7bb71f229952d30ad5f6fda26"} {"question" "q-64179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Homogeneous of degree $2$"] ["text" "Homogeneous of degree $3$"] ["text" "Homogeneous of degree $5$"] ["text" "Homogeneous of degree $6$"] ["text" "Not homogeneous"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64179" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "Not homogeneous"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Is the function $g(x,y,z)=2{x}^{2}+x{y}^{2}+5{z}^{2}$ homogeneous? If so, what is its degree?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A function $g(x,y,z)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\ng(tx,ty,tz)={t}^{n}g(x,y,z).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $g(tx,ty,tz),$ and then we simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}g(x,y,z)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(tx,ty,tz) & =2(tx)^{2}+(tx)(ty)^{2}+5(tz)^{2} \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}{x}^{2}+{t}^{3}x{y}^{2}+5{t}^{2}{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt's impossible to write this as\n\n$$\n{t}^{n}g(x,y,z)={t}^{n}(2{x}^{2}+x{y}^{2}+5{z}^{2})\n$$\n\nand so $g(x,y,z)$ is not homogeneous." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97da43b2889dff1e9a1bf9fcf026f3916bef5db7bb71f229952d30ad5f6fda26"} {"question" "q-90572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Homogeneous of degree $1$"] ["text" "Homogeneous of degree $2$"] ["text" "Homogeneous of degree $3$"] ["text" "Homogeneous of degree $4$"] ["text" "Not homogeneous"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "Not homogeneous"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64175" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Is the function $f(x,y,z)=3{x}^{2}+xy-4{z}^{2}$ homogeneous? If so, what is its degree?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64175" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A function $f(x,y,z)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty,tz)={t}^{n}f(x,y,z).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $f(tx,ty,tz),$ and then we simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}f(x,y,z)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty,tz) & =3(tx)^{2}+(tx)(ty)-4(tz)^{2} \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}{x}^{2}+{t}^{2}xy-4{t}^{2}{z}^{2} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}(3{x}^{2}+xy-4{z}^{2}) \\\\  & ={t}^{2}f(x,y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty,tz)={t}^{2}f(x,y,z)\n$$\n\nand so the degree of the homogeneous function $f(x,y,z)$ is $2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64175" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97da43b2889dff1e9a1bf9fcf026f3916bef5db7bb71f229952d30ad5f6fda26"} {"question" "q-64175" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64175" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Homogeneous of degree $1$"] ["text" "Homogeneous of degree $2$"] ["text" "Homogeneous of degree $3$"] ["text" "Homogeneous of degree $4$"] ["text" "Not homogeneous"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64175" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "Homogeneous of degree $2$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-79578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following polynomials are homogeneous?\n\n- $f(x)=3xy$\n- $g(x,y)={y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}y$\n- $h(x,y)={x}^{3}-4x{y}^{2}+3{y}^{3}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-79578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's go through each of the options.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is homogeneous of degree $2.$  It is a polynomial of degree $2,$ with no linear or constant terms.\n\n- The function $g(x,y)$ is not homogeneous. It is a polynomial of degree $3.$ However, it also contains a term $({y}^{2})$ that is of degree $2.$ Therefore, not all of its terms are of degree $3.$\n\n- The function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $3.$ It is a polynomial of degree $3,$ and all of its terms are of degree $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-79578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97da43b2889dff1e9a1bf9fcf026f3916bef5db7bb71f229952d30ad5f6fda26"} {"question" "q-79578" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-79578" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-79578" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64198" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following polynomials are homogeneous?\n\n- $f(y)=5{y}^{2}$\n- $g(x,y)=2{x}^{3}y+x{y}^{4}$\n- $h(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}+y{z}^{2}-xyz$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64198" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's go through each of the options.\n\n- The function $f(y)$ is homogeneous of degree $2.$ It is a polynomial of degree $2,$ with no linear or constant term.\n\n- The function $g(x,y)$ is not homogeneous. It is a polynomial of degree $5.$ However, it also contains a term ($2{x}^{3}y$) that is of degree $4.$ Therefore, not all of its terms are of degree $5.$\n\n- The function $h(x,y,z)$ is homogeneous of degree $3.$ It is a polynomial of degree $3,$ and all of its terms are of degree $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64198" "f