ough each of the options.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not homogeneous. It is a polynomial of degree $1.$ However, it also contains a constant term. Therefore not all of its terms are of degree $1.$\n\n- The function $g(x,y)$ is not homogeneous. It is a polynomial of degree $3.$ However, it also contains a term ($3xy$) that is of degree $2.$ Therefore, not all of its terms are of degree $3.$\n\n- The function $h(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $5.$ It is a polynomial of degree $5,$ and all of its terms are of degree $5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97da43b2889dff1e9a1bf9fcf026f3916bef5db7bb71f229952d30ad5f6fda26"} {"question" "q-64176" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64176" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64176" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90580" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following polynomials are homogeneous?\n\n- $f(x)=7{x}^{7}$\n- $g(x,y)=x+y$\n- $h(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z-2xyz+x{z}^{2}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90580" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's go through each of the options.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is homogeneous of degree $7.$  It is a polynomial of degree $7,$ with no terms of degree other than $7.$\n\n- The function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $1.$ It is a polynomial of degree $1,$ and all of its terms are of degree $1.$\n\n- The function $h(x,y,z)$ is  homogeneous of degree $3.$ It is a polynomial of degree $3,$ and all of its terms are of degree $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90580" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97da43b2889dff1e9a1bf9fcf026f3916bef5db7bb71f229952d30ad5f6fda26"} {"question" "q-90580" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90580" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90580" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90582" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following polynomials are homogeneous?\n\n- $f(y)={y}^{2}+y$\n- $g(x,y)={x}^{3}y+{y}^{4}$\n- $h(x,y,z)=xyz$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90582" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's go through each of the options.\n\n- The function $f(y)$  is not homogeneous. It is a polynomial of degree $2.$ However, it also contains a term ($y$) that is of degree $1.$ Therefore, not all of its terms are of degree $2.$\n\n- The function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $4.$ It is a polynomial of degree $4,$ and all of its terms are of degree $4.$\n\n- The function $h(x,y,z)$ is homogeneous of degree $3.$ It is a polynomial of degree $3,$ with no terms of degree other than $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90582" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97da43b2889dff1e9a1bf9fcf026f3916bef5db7bb71f229952d30ad5f6fda26"} {"question" "q-90582" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90582" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90582" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the degree of the homogeneous function $g(x,y)$ defined as\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=\\frac{x{y}^{3}}{4y-x}\\,?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nWe note that:\n\n- The numerator of $g(x,y)$ is a homogeneous polynomial of degree $4.$\n\n- The denominator of $g(x,y)$ is a homogeneous polynomial of degree $1.$\n\nTherefore, the function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $4-1=3.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nA function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\ng(tx,ty)={t}^{n}g(x,y).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $g(tx,ty),$ and then we simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}g(x,y)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(tx,ty) & =\\frac{(tx)(ty)^{3}}{4(ty)-(tx)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{4}x{y}^{3}}{4ty-tx} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{4}(x{y}^{3})}{t(4y-x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{4}}{t}\\cdot \\frac{x{y}^{3}}{4y-x} \\\\  & ={t}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{x{y}^{3}}{4y-x} \\\\  & ={t}^{3}g(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\ng(tx,ty)={t}^{3}g(x,y)\n$$\n\nand so the function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90589" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97da43b2889dff1e9a1bf9fcf026f3916bef5db7bb71f229952d30ad5f6fda26"} {"question" "q-90589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90589" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64199" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the degree of the homogeneous function $g(x,y)$ defined as\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=\\frac{xy-{x}^{2}}{3{y}^{2}}\\,?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64199" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nWe note that:\n\n- The numerator of $g(x,y)$ is a homogeneous polynomial of degree $2.$\n\n- The denominator of $g(x,y)$ is a homogeneous polynomial of degree $2.$\n\nTherefore, the function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $2-2=0.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nA function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\ng(tx,ty)={t}^{n}g(x,y).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $g(tx,ty),$ and then we simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}g(x,y)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(tx,ty) & =\\frac{(tx)(ty)-(tx)^{2}}{3(ty)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}xy-{t}^{2}{x}^{2}}{3{t}^{2}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}(xy-{x}^{2})}{{t}^{2}(3{x}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}}{{t}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{xy-{x}^{2}}{(3{x}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{xy-{x}^{2}}{(3{x}^{2})} \\\\  & =g(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${t}^{0}=1,$ the equality $g(tx,ty)=g(x,y)$ is equivalent to\n\n$$\ng(tx,ty)={t}^{0}g(x,y)\n$$\n\nand so the function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64199" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97da43b2889dff1e9a1bf9fcf026f3916bef5db7bb71f229952d30ad5f6fda26"} {"question" "q-64199" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64199" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64199" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the degree of the homogeneous function $f(x,y)$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{5{y}^{2}+xy}{2{x}^{4}}\\,?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nWe note that:\n\n- The numerator of $f(x,y)$ is a homogeneous polynomial of degree $2.$\n\n- The denominator of $f(x,y)$ is a homogeneous polynomial of degree $4.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $2-4=-2.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nA function $f(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty)={t}^{n}f(x,y).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $f(tx,ty),$ and then we simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}f(x,y)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =\\frac{5(ty)^{2}+(tx)(ty)}{2(tx)^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{t}^{2}{y}^{2}+{t}^{2}xy}{2{t}^{4}{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}(5{y}^{2}+xy)}{{t}^{4}(2{x}^{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{y}^{2}+xy}{{t}^{2}(2{x}^{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{5{y}^{2}+xy}{2{x}^{4}} \\\\  & ={t}^{-2}\\cdot \\frac{5{y}^{2}+xy}{2{x}^{4}} \\\\  & ={t}^{-2}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty)={t}^{-2}f(x,y)\n$$\n\nand so the function $f(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97da43b2889dff1e9a1bf9fcf026f3916bef5db7bb71f229952d30ad5f6fda26"} {"question" "q-64201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the degree of the homogeneous function $h(x,y)$ defined as\n\n$$\nh(x,y)=\\frac{x{y}^{3}+4{y}^{4}}{2{y}^{3}}\\,?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nWe note that:\n\n- The numerator of $h(x,y)$ is a homogeneous polynomial of degree $4.$\n\n- The denominator of $h(x,y)$ is a homogeneous polynomial of degree $3.$\n\nTherefore, the function $h(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $4-3=1.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nA function $h(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\nh(tx,ty)={t}^{n}h(x,y).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $h(tx,ty),$ and then we simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}h(x,y)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(tx,ty) & =\\frac{(tx)(ty)^{3}+4(ty)^{4}}{2(ty)^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{4}x{y}^{3}+4{t}^{4}{y}^{4}}{2{t}^{3}{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{4}(x{y}^{3}+4{y}^{4})}{{t}^{3}(2{y}^{3})} \\\\  & =t\\cdot \\frac{x{y}^{3}+4{y}^{4}}{2{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =t\\cdot \\frac{x{y}^{3}+4{y}^{4}}{2{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =th(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nh(tx,ty)=th(x,y)={t}^{1}h(x,y)\n$$\n\nand so the function $h(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97da43b2889dff1e9a1bf9fcf026f3916bef5db7bb71f229952d30ad5f6fda26"} {"question" "q-64200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the degree of the homogeneous function $g(x,y)$ defined as\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2xy-6{y}^{2}}\\,?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nWe note that:\n\n- The numerator of $g(x,y)$ is a homogeneous polynomial of degree $4.$\n\n- The denominator of $g(x,y)$ is a homogeneous polynomial of degree $2.$\n\nTherefore, the function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $4-2=2.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nA function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\ng(tx,ty)={t}^{n}g(x,y).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $g(tx,ty),$ and then we simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}g(x,y)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(tx,ty) & =\\frac{(tx)^{4}}{2(tx)(ty)-6(ty)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{4}{x}^{4}}{2{t}^{2}xy-6{t}^{2}{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{4}({x}^{4})}{{t}^{2}(2xy-6{y}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{4}}{{t}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{4}}{2xy-6{y}^{2}} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{4}}{2xy-6{y}^{2}} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}g(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\ng(tx,ty)={t}^{2}g(x,y)\n$$\n\nand so the function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90588" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97da43b2889dff1e9a1bf9fcf026f3916bef5db7bb71f229952d30ad5f6fda26"} {"question" "q-90588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90588" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the degree of the homogeneous function $g(x,y)=\\frac{4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3y}{x}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\ng(tx,ty)={t}^{n}g(x,y).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $g(tx,ty),$ and then we simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}g(x,y)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(tx,ty) & =\\frac{4(tx)^{2}-(ty)^{2}}{(tx)}\\,\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3ty}{tx}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4{t}^{2}{x}^{2}-{t}^{2}{y}^{2}}{tx}\\,\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3ty}{tx}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}(4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})}{tx}\\,\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}}{t}\\cdot \\frac{4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3y}{x}) \\\\  & =t\\cdot \\frac{4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3y}{x}) \\\\  & =tg(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\ng(tx,ty)=tg(x,y)={t}^{1}g(x,y)\n$$\n\nand so the degree of the homogeneous function $g(x,y)$ is $1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97da43b2889dff1e9a1bf9fcf026f3916bef5db7bb71f229952d30ad5f6fda26"} {"question" "q-90596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-79581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the degree of the homogeneous function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{3}-{x}^{3}}\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-79581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A function $f(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty)={t}^{n}f(x,y).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $h(tx,ty),$ and then we simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}f(x,y)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =\\frac{(tx)^{2}}{(ty)^{3}-(tx)^{3}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{tx}{ty}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}{x}^{2}}{{t}^{3}{y}^{3}-{t}^{3}{x}^{3}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{tx}{ty}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}{x}^{2}}{{t}^{3}({y}^{3}-{x}^{3})}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{tx}{ty}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}}{{t}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{3}-{x}^{3}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{3}-{x}^{3}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty)=\\frac{1}{t}\\cdot f(x,y)={t}^{-1}f(x,y)\n$$\n\nand so the degree of the homogeneous function $f(x,y)$ is $-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-79581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97da43b2889dff1e9a1bf9fcf026f3916bef5db7bb71f229952d30ad5f6fda26"} {"question" "q-79581" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-79581" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-79581" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90594" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the degree of the homogeneous function $f(x,y)=\\frac{x+3y}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2y}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90594" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A function $f(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty)={t}^{n}f(x,y).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $f(tx,ty),$ and then we simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}f(x,y)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =\\frac{tx+3ty}{(tx)^{2}(ty)^{2}}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{tx}{2ty}) \\\\  & =\\frac{t(x+3y)}{{t}^{4}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{t}{{t}^{4}}\\cdot \\frac{x+3y}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{x+3y}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2y}) \\\\  & ={t}^{-3}\\cdot \\frac{x+3y}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2y}) \\\\  & ={t}^{-3}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty)={t}^{-3}f(x,y)\n$$\n\nand so the degree of the homogeneous function $f(x,y)$ is $-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90594" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97da43b2889dff1e9a1bf9fcf026f3916bef5db7bb71f229952d30ad5f6fda26"} {"question" "q-90594" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90594" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-90594" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64202" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the degree of the homogeneous function $g(x,y)=\\frac{y}{3x-y}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64202" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A function $g(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\ng(tx,ty)={t}^{n}g(x,y).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $g(tx,ty),$ and then we simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}g(x,y)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(tx,ty) & =\\frac{ty}{3tx-ty}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{tx}{ty}) \\\\  & =\\frac{ty}{t(3x-y)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{tx}{ty}) \\\\  & =\\frac{t}{t}\\cdot \\frac{y}{3x-y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{3x-y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =g(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${t}^{0}=1,$ the equality $g(tx,ty)=g(x,y)$ is equivalent to\n\n$$\ng(tx,ty)=1\\cdot g(x,y)={t}^{0}g(x,y)\n$$\n\nand so the degree of the homogeneous function $g(x,y)$ is $0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64202" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97da43b2889dff1e9a1bf9fcf026f3916bef5db7bb71f229952d30ad5f6fda26"} {"question" "q-64202" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64202" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64202" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64204" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the degree of the homogeneous function $h(x,y)=\\frac{5y}{2{x}^{2}+8xy}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64204" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A function $h(x,y)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\nh(tx,ty)={t}^{n}h(x,y).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $h(tx,ty),$ and then we simplify by writing it as ${t}^{n}h(x,y)$ for some $n$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h(tx,ty) & =\\frac{5(ty)}{2(tx)^{2}+8(tx)(ty)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{tx}{ty}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5ty}{2{t}^{2}{x}^{2}+8{t}^{2}xy}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{tx}{ty}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5ty}{{t}^{2}(2{x}^{2}+8xy)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{tx}{ty}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5y}{t(2{x}^{2}+8xy)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\cdot \\frac{5y}{2{x}^{2}+8xy}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & ={t}^{-1}\\cdot \\frac{5y}{2{x}^{2}+8xy}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & ={t}^{-1}\\cdot h(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nh(tx,ty)=\\frac{1}{t}\\cdot h(x,y)={t}^{-1}h(x,y)\n$$\n\nand so the degree of the homogeneous function $h(x,y)$ is $-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64204" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "97da43b2889dff1e9a1bf9fcf026f3916bef5db7bb71f229952d30ad5f6fda26"} {"question" "q-64204" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64204" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "q-64204" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/state.json" "file_sha256" "4d3a24bdea6aaa89fdbfc4bedd2927e9d6399c80db3efdc70ce45136b9ff53d9"} {"question" "e-2298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Is the function $f(x,y,z) = x^3+2y^3+z^3$ homogeneous? If so, what is its degree?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/example-2298.json" "file_sha256" "30b16ef167070af7ffb0ba8f6a6385d44c8cd42713973925bb2b75f996d96533"} {"question" "e-2298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A function $f(x,y,z)$ is homogeneous of degree $n$ if it satisfies the property\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty, tz) = t^nf(x,y, z).\n$$\n\nSo first, we compute $f(tx,ty,tz),$ and then we simplify by writing it as $t^n f(x,y,z)$ for some $n\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty,tz) & =(tx)^{3}+2(ty)^{3}+(tz)^{3} \\\\  & ={t}^{3}{x}^{3}+2{t}^{3}{y}^{3}+{t}^{3}{z}^{3} \\\\  & ={t}^{3}({x}^{3}+2{y}^{3}+{z}^{3}) \\\\  & ={t}^{3}f(x,y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty,tz) = t^3 f(x,y,z)\n$$\n\nand so the function $f(x,y,z)$ is homogeneous of degree $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044049/example-2298.json" "file_sha256" "30b16ef167070af7ffb0ba8f6a6385d44c8cd42713973925bb2b75f996d96533"} {"question" "e-2300" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following polynomials are homogeneous?\n\n- $f(x,y) = x^2+x+y$\n\n- $g(x,y) = x^6-2x^3y^3 + y^6$\n\n- $h(x,y) = 6$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Acad